Scribbl/
│
├── index.html
│   # The landing page of the application where users log in or sign up.
│   # It connects to auth.js for handling authentication and redirects users to the dashboard after a successful login.
│
├── dashboard.html
│   # The main workspace shown after login.
│   # This page displays all user notes, secure notes, progress tracking, and settings.
│   # It links to the note templates and JavaScript modules that handle app interactions.
│
├── static/
│   # Contains all static assets such as stylesheets, scripts, images, and fonts used across the app.
│
│   ├── css/
│   │   ├── style.css         
│   │   │   # Defines the general visual styling shared across all pages (buttons, layouts, typography).
│   │   │
│   │   ├── auth.css          
│   │   │   # Handles the visual design for the login and signup forms on index.html.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── dashboard.css     
│   │   │   # Contains styles specifically for dashboard.html.
│   │   │   # Manages layout of the sidebar, note grid, modals, and responsive behavior.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── secure.css        
│   │   │   # Manages the look and feel of secure notes, password/pattern input modals, and locked views.
│   │   │
│   │   └── theme.css         
│   │       # Defines color themes (light and dark mode) and variables for consistent theming across the app.
│   │
│   ├── js/
│   │   ├── auth.js           
│   │   │   # Manages user authentication including login, signup, validation, and session control.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── main.js           
│   │   │   # Handles the core note logic — creating, editing, deleting, and saving notes.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── dashboard.js      
│   │   │   # Manages dashboard-specific behavior such as navigation, filtering notes, and updating UI states.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── ui.js             
│   │   │   # Handles rendering of dynamic UI elements and interactions such as modals, alerts, and card generation.
│   │   │
│   │   ├── progress.js       
│   │   │   # Controls progress tracking and data visualization (charts, analytics, and activity summaries).
│   │   │
│   │   ├── secure.js         
│   │   │   # Implements logic for secure notes — encryption, unlocking, and pattern/password verification.
│   │   │
│   │   └── utils.js          
│   │       # Contains helper functions used throughout the app (e.g., tag handling, data storage, date formatting).
│   │
│   ├── images/
│   │   ├── icons/            
│   │   │   # Contains icon assets used across the interface (buttons, actions, etc.).
│   │   │
│   │   └── logo.png          
│   │       # Application logo displayed on login and dashboard headers.
│   │
│   └── fonts/                
│       # Custom or imported fonts used for consistent typography.
│
├── templates/                
│   # Includes small, reusable HTML fragments that make up different interface components.
│   # These are loaded dynamically into the dashboard or other parts of the app.
│   │
│   ├── note_card.html        
│   │   # Template for displaying a single regular note with title, content, tags, and edit/delete options.
│   │
│   ├── secure_note_card.html 
│   │   # Similar to note_card but used for private, locked notes that require authentication to open.
│   │
│   ├── pattern_lock.html     
│   │   # Defines the visual layout and structure for the pattern lock system used to access secure notes.
│   │
│   ├── history_modal.html    
│   │   # Template for showing note history or progress tracking in a popup modal.
│   │
│   ├── settings_panel.html   
│   │   # Contains the structure for user settings such as theme, layout, and account preferences.
│   │
│   └── auth_form.html        
│       # Reusable structure for login and signup forms, allowing consistent design and easy updates.
│
├── assets/                   
│   # Stores additional media, illustrations, or background images used in the app.
│
├── app.py (optional)         
│   # Optional backend written in Python (Flask).
│   # Can be used for encrypted data handling, user account storage, or AI-based features in the future.
│
└── README.md                 
    # Documentation file that explains project overview, features, setup guide, and contribution details.

